speechtext:
I have the honour to inform the House that a message has been received from the Senate informing this House that the Senate has passed Bill C-35, an Act for granting to Her Majesty certain sums of money for the Government of Canada for the financial year ending March 31, 1987.
I also have the honour to inform the House that a message has been received from the Senate informing this House that the Senate has passed the following Bills, without amendment:
Bill C-14, an Act to amend the Excise Tax Act and the Excise Act;
Bill C-16, an Act to amend the Unemployment Insurance Act, 1971;
Bill C-17, an Act to amend the Petroleum and Gas Revenue Tax Act and the Income Tax Act and to repeal the Petroleum and Gas Revenue Gas Tax Act;
Bill C-23, an Act to amend the Income Tax Act and a related Act;
Bill C-25, an Act to authorize the divestiture of Canadair Limited and to provide for other matters in connection therewith;

Mr. Speaker, there has been discussion with the House Leaders of the other two Parties and I think you will find acceptance to the following motion being put:
That when the House adjourns this day, it shall stand adjourned until 11 o'clock a.m. on Monday, January 19, 1987;
That, for the purposes of Standing Order 4, the first sitting day in 1987, shall be deemed to have been January 12, 1987;
That on Monday, January 19, 1987, the House shall continue to sit between the hours of 6 o'clock p.m. and 9 o'clock p.m. for the purpose of considering Government Orders;
That on Tuesday, January 20 and Thursday, January 22, 1987, the House shall continue to sit between the hours of 1 o'clock p.m. and 2 o'clock p.m., and 6 o'clock p.m. and 9 o'clock p.m. for the purpose of considering Government Orders; and
Bill C-36, an Act to amend the Salaries Act.
